<newsitem itemid="50052" id="root" date="1996-09-12" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Utd News H1 pretax, pre-excep 151 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Utd News H1 pretax, pre-excep 151 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p>Pre-excep shr (pence)   21.1		   vs 16.9</p>
<p>Dividend (pence)	  8.0		    vs n/a</p>
<p>Pretax, pre-excep	151.9		   vs 125.0</p>
<p>Turnover		   1,039.2		 vs 944.7</p>
<p>NOTE - United News &amp; Media completed a merger with MAI Plc in April. The comparative figures have been restated to take account of the merger.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 159.9		 vs 132.0</p>
<p> Exceptional costs	 32.3		 vs 12.7</p>
<p> Interest payable	   8.0		 vs 7.0</p>
<p> Pre-tax, post-excep    119.6		 vs 112.3</p>
<p> Tax			   38.8		 vs 36.2</p>
<p> Net taxed		   80.8		 vs 76.1</p>
<p> Retained		    79.1		 vs 78.8</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 2</p>
<p>Div registration date  October 15  Ex-div date		October 7</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 105.7 to 144.0 million stg. United News said a 32 million stg cost on the reorganisation of Express Newspapers and an 82 million stg profit on the sale of Tolley Publishing would be included in the full-year results.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
